# Wooden Void Excavator tooltip
vmd.excavator.desc.1=Non-electric wooden excavator that digs plain (non ore) resource blocks of a chosen dimension out of the void; the resource tables are config driven.
vmd.excavator.desc.2=The second input slot takes a dimension display block to select the dimension (not consumed); an empty slot means the Overworld default resources.
vmd.excavator.desc.3=Produces 1 resource block every 200 ticks into one of its 6 output slots (same items stack up); the machine stalls when none of the 6 output slots can hold more output, take the outputs out manually or with a conveyor.
vmd.excavator.desc.4=The programmed circuit (configuration 1..N) can be configured directly in the circuit slot in the GUI (or a real programmed circuit can be inserted there) to select the N-th resource of that dimension's table; configuration 0 or no circuit = weighted random (weights = table weights).
vmd.excavator.desc.5=A circuit configuration beyond the resource count idles the machine; resource tables are configured in cheapervoidminers.cfg, category excavator_resources.
vmd.excavator.desc.selection=Current selection: %s

# Void Excavator tooltip (multiblock)
vmd.mbe.machine_type=Void Excavator
vmd.mbe.info.1=Digs plain (non ore) resource blocks of a chosen dimension out of the void; the resource tables are config driven (cheapervoidminers.cfg, category excavator_resources).
vmd.mbe.info.2=The dimension display block in the controller slot selects the dimension; leave the slot empty to use the dimension the machine is built in.
vmd.mbe.info.3=A programmed circuit (configuration 1..N) in the input bus selects the N-th resource of that dimension's table; configuration 0 or no circuit picks a resource by weighted random (weights = table weights).
vmd.mbe.info.4=A circuit configuration beyond the resource count of the dimension fails the cycle with an error message.
vmd.mbe.info.5=Drill heads in the input bus boost the output: Iron x1.25, Steel x1.5, Titanium x1.75, Naquadah x2.0, Infinity x3.0 (highest present applies). Each finished cycle consumes one drill head with a 0.1% chance.
vmd.mbe.info.6=Produces %s resource block(s) x parallel count x drill bonus per 100 tick cycle.
vmd.mbe.structure.input_bus=Input Bus (dimension display, drill head and programmed circuit)
vmd.mbe.structure.output_bus=Output Bus (resource output, required)

